    "methodology_summary": "Cryptocurrency portfolios are formed using bivariate sorts on past cumulative returns (momentum) and Amihud illiquidity measures over a 14-day lookback period. Selected cryptocurrencies are divided into 3 momentum groups and 3 illiquidity groups to form 9 equal-weighted portfolios, rebalanced bi-weekly (every 14 days). Long-only strategies (illiquid losers and liquid winners) and zero-investment factor portfolios (UMD and IML) are evaluated against a market capitalization-weighted benchmark.",
