    "key_findings": [
      "A strong and statistically significant momentum effect is observed in the most liquid cryptocurrencies, supporting investor herding theories.",
      "Illiquidity is most profitable among the previous period's loser cryptocurrencies, exhibiting a significant illiquidity premium.",
      "Illiquid cryptocurrencies display a mean reversion effect, where illiquid losers outperform illiquid winners.",
      "Two long-only strategies (liquid winners and illiquid losers) show improved risk-adjusted performance over the market capitalization-weighted benchmark even when factoring in trading costs."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Illiquid losers portfolio performance may deteriorate in practice due to higher indirect trading costs and bid-ask spreads in illiquid cryptocurrencies."
    ],
